**Problem 10.2.** Given that
(a) $x^2+y^2+2z^2$ represents all integers not of the form $4^m(16n+14)$;
(b) $x^2+y^2+3z^2$ represents all integers not of the form $9^m(9n+6)$;
(c) $x^2+2y^2+2z^2$ represents all integers not of the form $4^m(8n+7)$;
(d) $x^2+2y^2+3z^2$ represents all integers not of the form $4^m(16n+10)$;
(e) $x^2+2y^2+4z^2$ represents all integers not of the form $4^m(16n+14)$;
(f) $x^2+2y^2+5z^2$ represents all integers not of the form $25^m(25n+10)$ or $25^m(25n+15)$,
classify all universal conic polynomials of the form $ax^2+by^2+cz^2+dw^2$ (positive integers $a\le b\le c\le d$). (Use also Problems 9.1 and 10.1; $x^2+y^2+z^2$ misses exactly $4^m(8n+7)$.)
